WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.807
A useful way to learn NumPy is to think of it as a workflow.

00:00:04.807 --> 00:00:07.542
First, create or load numerical data.

00:00:07.542 --> 00:00:11.912
Second, inspect the array so you understand its structure.

00:00:11.912 --> 00:00:19.682
Then transform or calculate values, select the values you need, and reshape the array if the analysis requires a

00:00:19.682 --> 00:00:21.646
different organization.

00:00:22.452 --> 00:00:27.904
After that, summarize the data and check whether the results make sense.

00:00:27.904 --> 00:00:30.054
This order is important.

00:00:30.054 --> 00:00:39.744
For example, before calculating an average across columns, you should know what each column represents and which axis

00:00:39.744 --> 00:00:44.949
you are using. Many mistakes with NumPy come from skipping the inspection step.

00:00:44.949 --> 00:00:53.757
So throughout this module, we will repeatedly check shape, dimensions, and data type before performing calculations.
